# PATCH: 017-compile-in-lockprefs
#
# Compiles the contents of config/mozilla.cfg directly into libxul as a
# function that runs at pref-service startup, eliminating DenBrowser's
# dependency on the on-disk mozilla.cfg and autoconfig.js files for the
# lockPref enforcement layer.
#
# Without this patch, the autoconfig lockdown is enforced by two files
# sitting next to the application binary:
#
#   <install>/mozilla.cfg              — the lockPref() calls themselves
#   <install>/defaults/pref/autoconfig.js — tells Firefox to load mozilla.cfg
#
# An admin (or anything running with admin privileges) can swap mozilla.cfg
# for a permissive version, delete autoconfig.js so mozilla.cfg never loads,
# or both — and on the next launch every lockPref is gone.  That defeats
# layer 4 of the four-layer defense model entirely with a two-file edit.
#
# With this patch, the same set of locks lives in xul.dll/libxul.so.  An
# attacker would need to modify the linked library — a much higher bar than
# editing a text file, and one that breaks any code-signing scheme applied
# to the build output.  The on-disk mozilla.cfg is still shipped as belt-
# and-suspenders, but it is no longer the only enforcement of these prefs.
#
# Implementation:
#
#   The body of SetupDenBrowserLockdown() is generated by
#   scripts/gen-017-patch.sh from config/mozilla.cfg.  Each lockPref() call
#   in the .cfg becomes a SetBool/SetInt/SetCString call (PrefValueKind::
#   Default) followed by Preferences::Lock(name).  The generator preserves
#   one source of truth — edit mozilla.cfg, re-run the generator, rebuild.
#
#   The function is called from Preferences::GetInstanceForService(), in
#   the parent-process branch, immediately after pref-config-startup has
#   run.  Running after pref-config-startup means our compiled-in values
#   overwrite any value mozilla.cfg may have set (and re-lock the pref),
#   so a tampered on-disk mozilla.cfg cannot win.  Running in the parent
#   process only is fine — child processes inherit prefs via IPC and the
#   locked state propagates with them.
#
# Regeneration:
#
#   Run scripts/gen-017-patch.sh after editing config/mozilla.cfg, or after
#   bumping the Firefox ESR version if the sentinels in Preferences.cpp
#   have shifted.  The script verifies the patch applies cleanly before
#   overwriting the diff section of this file.

